    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature for pet owners. The request may include an optional `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the response now returns `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so the title survives a create \u2192 save \u2192 read-back round trip.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** (spec, drives DTO generation) \u2014\n   - Added `title` as an optional input property on `OwnerFields`.\n   - Added `salutation` as a read-only derived property on `Owner`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** (MapStruct) \u2014 added a `salutation` mapping that composes `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to just `lastName` when the title is null or blank. The inbound `title` auto-maps by name into the `Owner` entity.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table so persistence works across all supported databases (the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\nThe new acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` passes (verifies `salutation == \"DR who\"`), and the full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.",
